79c77e3eeb53"}], "patch": "patches/2d83a3da281266aeb2928272001043ecc04a8fe4-1/20260924T001959Z-28e8c5a7.patch", "provenance": "verbatim", "runs": {}, "test_sources": [{"commit": "2d83a3da281266aeb2928272001043ecc04a8fe4", "paths": ["src/block/compress.rs"]}], "tests": ["block::compress::tests::test_dict_no_panic"]}, "shard": "lz4_flex", "status": "blocked", "subject": "Fix: Small dict leads to panic", "summary": "Compression with a three-byte dictionary reaches a four-byte candidate read in get_batch, causing an out-of-bounds panic with default safe-encode enabled. The fix treats dictionaries shorter than the four-byte minimum match as empty. The regression test added by the fix exercises this case. The proposed reversal restores the exact parent implementation while preserving the test; reproduction has not been run.", "updated_at": "2026-09-24T00:22:37.507707+00:00"}
