f758a09a4a916de927d1c1034478f1d904fd1f08-1/20260924T173309Z-41c2f424.patch", "provenance": "verbatim", "runs": {}, "test_sources": [{"commit": "f758a09a4a916de927d1c1034478f1d904fd1f08", "paths": ["src/block/decompress.rs"]}], "tests": ["bug_fuzz_8"]}, "shard": "lz4_flex", "status": "blocked", "subject": "Fix an issue for output buffer pointer underflow", "summary": "The decoder subtracts the dictionary safety margin directly from an output pointer, potentially moving it before the allocation. With a zero-capacity output buffer, the pointer can wrap and incorrectly permit the fast decoding loop, causing a panic instead of returning an output-size error. The fix uses saturating integer subtraction before constructing the pointer. The fix-added root-level integration test bug_fuzz_8 in tests/tests.rs exercises this case. It requires checked-decode enabled and safe-decode disabled; select it with cargo test --no-default-features --features std,safe-encode,checked-decode --test tests bug_fuzz_8 -- --exact. No tests were executed.", "updated_at": "2026-09-24T17:35:58.572494+00:00"}
